# DIPR slides: no small sub-text

The deck is presented on a screen; small secondary lines cannot be read.

- Do not add small explanatory sub-lines under headings, banners, chips, steps or cards
  (e.g. a one-line description under "One Platform. Complete Advertising Lifecycle.",
  or a paragraph under the slide subtitle).
- Do not invent extra copy. Use only the content the user provides for the slide.
- Every visible text should be at least ~13px at 1440x900 (`clamp(13px, ...)` minimum).
- Prefer one strong heading plus short labels over heading + small paragraph.

```tsx
// BAD: small sub-line under a heading
<span className="text-[length:clamp(10px,1.4vh,13px)] text-white/75">A centralized, secure ...</span>

// GOOD: heading only, readable size
<span className="font-display text-[length:clamp(16px,2.4vh,22px)] font-bold">One Platform. Complete Advertising Lifecycle.</span>
```
